d. allocating budget for the provision of protection for women and children victims of violence; and

e. fostering and supervising the provision of protection for women and children victims of violence. (2) In carrying out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Mayor shall establish programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in one Regional Action Plan as a basis for Regional Agencies in implementing the protection of women and children victims of violence.

